I couldn't find an existing signal engine script: this repo was empty and I had no saved notes from earlier sessions. So I wrote one. It's two files you paste into Google Apps Script, which is free and runs in your Google account, so no server is needed.

- `Code.gs`: the script
- `appsscript.json`: settings, with the time zone set to Europe/London

**What it does each morning**
1. Reads every email under **Signals** from the last 3 days that hasn't already been in a digest.
2. Gives each email a score for two topics:
   - **Lease and tenancy law**, matching phrases like "Renters' Rights", "section 21", "leasehold", "ground rent", "selective licensing", "Awaab's Law", "EPC" and "tribunal".
   - **Council planning notices**, matching phrases like "planning application", "prior approval", "Article 4", "change of use", "Class C4", "conservation area" and "weekly list".

   A topic word in the subject line is worth 3 points and each different topic word in the body is worth 1. An email needs at least 2 points to count.
3. Sends you one email with a section for each topic, best matches first. Each entry shows the sender, a short quote around the matching words and a link to the original. Everything else is listed in one line each at the bottom.
4. Puts a **Signals/Digested** label on everything it read, so nothing appears in two digests. It doesn't archive anything or mark it read unless you switch that on.

## Setup (about 10 minutes)

1. **Create the project.** Go to [script.google.com](https://script.google.com) while signed in to the Gmail account that has the Signals label. Click **New project** and name it "Signal Engine".
2. **Paste the code.** Replace everything in the editor's `Code.gs` with the contents of `Code.gs` from this folder.
3. **Paste the settings.** Click ⚙️ **Project Settings** and tick **Show "appsscript.json" manifest file in editor**. Go back to the editor, open `appsscript.json` and replace its contents with the file from this folder.
4. **Check the settings at the top of `Code.gs`.**
   - `sourceLabel: 'Signals'` must match your label exactly.
   - Leave `recipient` blank to send the digest to yourself, or put in another address.
   - `digestHour: 7` sets the delivery time to around 7am. Google runs it at some point within that hour.
5. **Do a test run.** Choose **`previewDigest`** from the function menu and click **Run**.
   - Google will ask for permission the first time. Choose your account, click **Advanced**, then **Go to Signal Engine (unsafe)**. The warning appears because Google hasn't reviewed the script, but it's your own code running in your own account. Then click **Allow**.
   - You should get an email titled **[PREVIEW] Signals digest**. The preview doesn't label anything, so you can run it as often as you like.
6. **Adjust the topics if needed.** If something irrelevant gets through, remove the word that caught it from the `keywords` list. If something you care about is missed, add the phrase it uses (in lowercase). Run `previewDigest` again to check.
7. **Turn it on.** Choose **`installTrigger`** and click **Run** once. It will then run every day by itself. You can confirm under ⏰ **Triggers** in the left sidebar. To stop it, run **`removeTrigger`**.

## Good to know
- **Your first real digest** will include up to 3 days of backlog. After that it covers about one day.
- **Errors:** if a run fails, Google emails you by default. Run history is under **Executions**.
- **Missed days:** if a run is skipped, the next one picks up those emails, as long as they're less than 3 days old (`lookbackDays`).
- **UK terms:** I assumed English tenancy and planning terms. If you're in Scotland, add phrases like "private residential tenancy" and "First-tier Tribunal (Housing and Property Chamber)".
- **Not tested yet:** this is a first version, and I couldn't run any check on the code in my environment. Your step 5 preview will be its first real run, so if it shows an error, send me the message and I'll fix it.

If you'd like plain-English summaries instead of quotes, I can add an AI summary step. That needs an API key and costs a small amount per day.
--- appsscript.json ---
{
  "timeZone": "Europe/London",
  "dependencies": {},
  "exceptionLogging": "STACKDRIVER",
  "runtimeVersion": "V8"
}

--- Code.gs ---
/**
 * Signal Engine — Harbourside Lettings
 *
 * Reads everything under the Gmail label "Signals", scores each thread against
 * the topics below, and sends one daily digest email. Threads that have been
 * included in a digest get the label "Signals/Digested" so they never repeat.
 *
 * Entry points (run these from the Apps Script editor):
 *   previewDigest()  - emails you a digest WITHOUT labelling anything (safe test)
 *   runDigest()      - the real run; the daily trigger calls this
 *   installTrigger() - schedules runDigest() once a day
 *   removeTrigger()  - stops the schedule
 */

const CONFIG = {
  sourceLabel: 'Signals',
  doneLabel: 'Signals/Digested',
  // Leave blank to send to the account that owns the script.
  recipient: '',
  digestHour: 7, // 24h clock, in the time zone set in appsscript.json
  lookbackDays: 3, // safety window in case a run is missed
  maxThreads: 150,
  minScore: 2, // a thread needs at least this score to count as a match
  sendWhenEmpty: true, // still send a short "nothing relevant" note
  archiveAfterDigest: false, // true = also remove from inbox once digested
  markReadAfterDigest: false,

  // Subject hit = 3 points, each distinct keyword found in the body = 1 point.
  // Keywords are matched case-insensitively as plain phrases.
  topics: [
    {
      name: 'Lease & tenancy law',
      keywords: [
        "renters' rights", 'renters rights', 'section 21', 'section 8',
        'section 13', 'assured shorthold', 'assured tenancy', 'periodic tenancy',
        'tenancy agreement', 'leasehold', 'freehold', 'ground rent',
        'service charge', 'deposit protection', 'tenancy deposit', 'rent increase',
        'rent repayment order', 'possession order', 'possession claim', 'eviction',
        'selective licensing', 'additional licensing', 'landlord licensing',
        'hmo licen', 'decent homes', "awaab's law", 'awaabs law', 'epc',
        'minimum energy efficiency', 'mees', 'landlord database', 'prs database',
        'ombudsman', 'right to rent', 'legislation', 'statutory instrument',
        'royal assent', 'commencement', 'court of appeal', 'upper tribunal',
        'first-tier tribunal',
      ],
    },
    {
      name: 'Council planning notices',
      keywords: [
        'planning application', 'planning permission', 'planning notice',
        'planning consultation', 'decision notice', 'prior approval',
        'permitted development', 'article 4', 'change of use', 'use class',
        'class c4', 'conservation area', 'listed building', 'local plan',
        'neighbourhood plan', 'planning appeal', 'enforcement notice',
        'section 106', 's106', 'community infrastructure levy', 'cil',
        'planning committee', 'development management', 'site notice',
        'weekly list', 'validated applications',
      ],
    },
  ],
};

function runDigest() {
  buildAndSend_({ dryRun: false });
}

function previewDigest() {
  buildAndSend_({ dryRun: true });
}

function installTrigger() {
  removeTrigger();
  ScriptApp.newTrigger('runDigest')
    .timeBased()
    .everyDays(1)
    .atHour(CONFIG.digestHour)
    .create();
  Logger.log('Daily trigger installed for about %s:00 (%s).',
      CONFIG.digestHour, Session.getScriptTimeZone());
}

function removeTrigger() {
  ScriptApp.getProjectTriggers()
    .filter(t => t.getHandlerFunction() === 'runDigest')
    .forEach(t => ScriptApp.deleteTrigger(t));
}

function buildAndSend_({ dryRun }) {
  const source = GmailApp.getUserLabelByName(CONFIG.sourceLabel);
  if (!source) throw new Error(`Gmail label "${CONFIG.sourceLabel}" not found.`);
  const done = GmailApp.getUserLabelByName(CONFIG.doneLabel) ||
      GmailApp.createLabel(CONFIG.doneLabel);

  const query = `label:${quoteLabel_(CONFIG.sourceLabel)} ` +
      `-label:${quoteLabel_(CONFIG.doneLabel)} newer_than:${CONFIG.lookbackDays}d`;
  const threads = GmailApp.search(query, 0, CONFIG.maxThreads);

  const buckets = CONFIG.topics.map(t => ({ topic: t, items: [] }));
  const other = [];

  threads.forEach(thread => {
    const msg = thread.getMessages().pop();
    const item = {
      threadId: thread.getId(),
      subject: msg.getSubject() || '(no subject)',
      from: msg.getFrom().replace(/<.*>/, '').replace(/"/g, '').trim(),
      date: msg.getDate(),
    };
    const subject = item.subject.toLowerCase();
    const body = msg.getPlainBody().slice(0, 20000);
    const bodyLower = body.toLowerCase();

    let best = null;
    buckets.forEach(bucket => {
      const hits = bucket.topic.keywords.filter(k =>
          containsPhrase_(subject, k) || containsPhrase_(bodyLower, k));
      if (!hits.length) return;
      const subjectHit = bucket.topic.keywords.some(k => containsPhrase_(subject, k));
      const score = (subjectHit ? 3 : 0) + hits.length;
      if (score >= CONFIG.minScore && (!best || score > best.score)) {
        best = { bucket, score, hits };
      }
    });

    if (best) {
      best.bucket.items.push(Object.assign(item, {
        score: best.score,
        hits: best.hits.slice(0, 5),
        snippet: snippetAround_(body, bodyLower, best.hits),
      }));
    } else {
      other.push(item);
    }
  });

  buckets.forEach(b => b.items.sort((a, z) => z.score - a.score));
  const matched = buckets.reduce((n, b) => n + b.items.length, 0);

  if (matched || CONFIG.sendWhenEmpty) {
    const tz = Session.getScriptTimeZone();
    const today = Utilities.formatDate(new Date(), tz, 'EEE d MMM yyyy');
    const subject = `${dryRun ? '[PREVIEW] ' : ''}Signals digest — ${today} ` +
        `(${matched} relevant of ${threads.length})`;
    GmailApp.sendEmail(recipient_(), subject, plainText_(buckets, other), {
      htmlBody: html_(buckets, other, threads.length, today, tz),
      name: 'Signal Engine',
    });
  }

  if (!dryRun && threads.length) {
    // addToThreads is capped at 100 threads per call.
    for (let i = 0; i < threads.length; i += 100) {
      const batch = threads.slice(i, i + 100);
      done.addToThreads(batch);
      if (CONFIG.archiveAfterDigest) GmailApp.moveThreadsToArchive(batch);
      if (CONFIG.markReadAfterDigest) GmailApp.markThreadsRead(batch);
    }
  }

  Logger.log('%s threads scanned, %s relevant, dryRun=%s', threads.length, matched, dryRun);
}

function containsPhrase_(text, phrase) {
  // Word-boundary match so short keywords like "epc" or "cil" don't fire inside other words.
  const escaped = phrase.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, '\\$&');
  return new RegExp(`(^|[^a-z0-9])${escaped}`, 'i').test(text);
}

function snippetAround_(body, bodyLower, hits) {
  for (const k of hits) {
    const i = bodyLower.indexOf(k);
    if (i >= 0) {
      const start = Math.max(0, i - 120);
      const text = body.slice(start, i + k.length + 180).replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
      return (start > 0 ? '… ' : '') + text + ' …';
    }
  }
  return body.slice(0, 250).replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim() + ' …';
}

function html_(buckets, other, scanned, today, tz) {
  const link = id => `https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/${id}`;
  const section = b => {
    if (!b.items.length) {
      return `<h2 style="font-size:16px;margin:24px 0 8px">${esc_(b.topic.name)}</h2>` +
          '<p style="color:#666;margin:0">Nothing today.</p>';
    }
    return `<h2 style="font-size:16px;margin:24px 0 8px">${esc_(b.topic.name)} (${b.items.length})</h2>` +
        b.items.map(it => `
          <div style="margin:0 0 14px;padding:10px 12px;border-left:3px solid #1a73e8;background:#f6f8fc">
            <a href="${link(it.threadId)}" style="font-weight:600;color:#1a73e8;text-decoration:none">${esc_(it.subject)}</a>
            <div style="font-size:12px;color:#666;margin:2px 0 6px">${esc_(it.from)} · ${Utilities.formatDate(it.date, tz, 'd MMM HH:mm')} · matched: ${esc_(it.hits.join(', '))}</div>
            <div style="font-size:13px;color:#333">${esc_(it.snippet)}</div>
          </div>`).join('');
  };
  const otherList = other.length
    ? `<h2 style="font-size:14px;margin:24px 0 8px;color:#666">Everything else (${other.length})</h2><ul style="font-size:12px;color:#666;padding-left:18px">` +
      other.map(it => `<li><a href="${link(it.threadId)}" style="color:#666">${esc_(it.subject)}</a> — ${esc_(it.from)}</li>`).join('') +
      '</ul>'
    : '';
  return `<div style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif;max-width:680px">
    <h1 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 4px">Signals digest</h1>
    <div style="color:#666;font-size:13px">${today} · ${scanned} emails scanned</div>
    ${buckets.map(section).join('')}
    ${otherList}
  </div>`;
}

function plainText_(buckets, other) {
  const lines = [];
  buckets.forEach(b => {
    lines.push(`== ${b.topic.name} (${b.items.length}) ==`);
    b.items.forEach(it => lines.push(`- ${it.subject} [${it.from}]`, `  ${it.snippet}`));
    lines.push('');
  });
  lines.push(`Everything else: ${other.length} emails`);
  return lines.join('\n');
}

function recipient_() {
  return CONFIG.recipient || Session.getEffectiveUser().getEmail();
}

function quoteLabel_(name) {
  // Gmail search wants spaces and slashes in label names as hyphens.
  return name.replace(/[\s/]+/g, '-');
}

function esc_(s) {
  return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g, c =>
      ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;' })[c]);
}

