# Northgate Cycles – service reminder letters

Google Apps Script that makes one filled-in copy of the service reminder Doc
template for every customer in the sheet.

## One-time setup

1. **Check the sheet.** The customer tab (default name `Customers`) needs these
   headers in row 1, in any order: `first_name`, `bike`, `due_date`. Other
   columns are ignored. Format `due_date` as a date. The script adds `doc_url` and
   `status` columns on its first run.
2. **Check the template.** The Doc should contain `{{first_name}}`, `{{bike}}` and
   `{{due_date}}`. They can appear in the body, header or footer and keep whatever
   formatting you give them.
3. **Make an output folder** in Drive for the letters.
4. **Add the script.** In the sheet, open **Extensions → Apps Script**. Paste
   `Code.gs` over the default `Code.gs`. To use the manifest, turn on
   **Project Settings → Show "appsscript.json"** and paste `appsscript.json` too.
   Change its `timeZone` if you aren't in the UK.
5. **Fill in `CONFIG`** at the top of `Code.gs`:
   - `TEMPLATE_DOC_ID`: the long ID in the template's URL
     (`docs.google.com/document/d/<ID>/edit`)
   - `OUTPUT_FOLDER_ID`: the ID in the folder's URL
     (`drive.google.com/drive/folders/<ID>`)
   - `SHEET_NAME`, `DATE_FORMAT` and `FILE_NAME` if the defaults don't suit
6. Save, then reload the sheet. A **Service letters** menu appears.

## Running it

1. **Service letters → Generate test letter (first pending row).** The first
   time, Google asks you to authorise the script. After that it creates one
   letter. Open the link in `doc_url` and check the wording and the date format.
2. If the test letter looks wrong, fix the template or `CONFIG`, delete the test
   Doc, and clear that row's `doc_url`.
3. **Service letters → Generate all letters.** Each row gets a Doc link and a
   `Created …` timestamp.

The 180 rows probably won't finish inside Apps Script's 6-minute limit. When a
run gets close to the limit, it stops by itself and schedules a follow-up run
about a minute later, so you can close the sheet and let it finish. It's done
when every row has a `doc_url`.

## Re-running and fixing problems

- Rows that already have a `doc_url` are skipped, so running it again is safe.
  New customers added later get letters on the next run.
- If a row says `ERROR: …` (usually `missing due_date`, or another blank cell),
  fix the cell and run **Generate all letters** again. Only that row is retried.
- To regenerate everything (for example after changing the template), use
  **Clear status (start over)**. Old Docs stay in Drive, so delete or move them
  first if you don't want duplicates.
- Only one run can happen at a time. If you click while a run is going, you'll
  get a "run already in progress" message.

